            <ArticleTitle>C. difficile PCR-ribotype 023 might go undetected when using ChromId C. difficile agar.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>34-35</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1075-9964(17)30016-1</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.anaerobe.2017.01.008</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We compared the performance of the new chromogenic medium ChromID C. difficile with that of CLO agar. ChromID C. difficile agar is a sensitive medium that can accelerate the presumptive identification of C. difficile, however ribotype 023 might go undetected when using this chromogenic medium.</AbstractText>
